A FAIR data product's signing & trust lifecycle, through four hands. Runs the real `tessera` binary
against a fixture `study.tsra` (a sealed recon product, as if freshly acquired). Random key material is
globbed with `[..]`; everything else is the verbatim transcript.

# === Instrument scientist — generate a signing key, sign the study at the source (air-gapped OK). ===

```
$ tessera keygen instrument.key
wrote private key instrument.key (keep secret — mode 0600)
wrote public  key instrument.key.pub (share freely)
  key_id [..]

```

```
$ tessera sign study.tsra --key instrument.key --signer https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097
OK  signed study.tsra
  embedded  aux/signatures/[..].sig.json
  key_id    [..]
  key_fmt   raw-hex
  signed_at [..]
  signer    https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097

```

# === Data scientist — refuses an unknown key: untrusted until the custodian vets it. ===

```
$ tessera verify-sig study.tsra
? failed
error: [..]untrusted: key_id [..]is not in any consulted trust store[..]

```

# === Data custodian — vets + trusts the instrument's key in the repo-local store. ===

```
$ tessera trust add instrument.key.pub --name instrument-lab --signer https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097 --repo
trusted 'instrument-lab'  key_id [..]  signer https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097
note: .tessera/trust is not consulted implicitly — pass `verify-sig --trust-dir .tessera/trust`, or set TESSERA_TRUST_DIR=$PWD/.tessera/trust (absolute) if you mean it, for it to take effect

```

```
$ tessera trust list --repo
.tessera/trust (repo store)
  instrument-lab   [..]  https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097
note: .tessera/trust is not consulted implicitly — pass `verify-sig --trust-dir .tessera/trust`, or set TESSERA_TRUST_DIR=$PWD/.tessera/trust (absolute) if you mean it, for it to take effect

```

# A store in the current directory is never trusted on its own — whoever can write to the directory a
# verifier runs in could plant a key there. Name it with `--trust-dir` (or `TESSERA_TRUST_DIR`):

```
$ tessera verify-sig study.tsra
? failed
error: [..]untrusted: key_id [..]is not in any consulted trust store[..]

```

```
$ tessera verify-sig study.tsra --trust-dir .tessera/trust
OK  study.tsra — trusted as 'instrument-lab' + 1 blocks intact
  signer https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097 (attribution; not a trust anchor)
accepted key_id [..] via trust store [..]/.tessera/trust (--trust-dir)

```

# === Researcher / auditor — a signer-policy mismatch is rejected (attribution is checked too). ===

```
$ tessera verify-sig study.tsra --trust-dir .tessera/trust --require-signer https://orcid.org/9999-9999-9999-9999
? failed
error: invalid product: signer policy: required 'https://orcid.org/9999-9999-9999-9999', sidecar attributes to Some("https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097")

```

# === Automated verifier — pins the key AND the signer, consulting no store at all. ===

```
$ tessera verify-sig study.tsra --pubkey instrument.key.pub --require-signer https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097
OK  study.tsra — explicit --pubkey + 1 blocks intact
  signer https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097 (attribution; not a trust anchor)
accepted key_id [..] via --pubkey instrument.key.pub

```
